{"type": "final", "turn": 6, "content": "\n\nBoth predictions are completed and I compared them over your PA Karst area (shared extent ~10,091 km\u00b2), sampled on a 6x6 grid:\n\n- **Different properties, not the same quantity**: KarstBinary outputs `sample_karst_score` (0\u20131); KarstNumber outputs `sample_number` (0.2\u20131.2). So only their co-variation is meaningful.\n- **They barely agree spatially**: correlation **-0.017** across the 25 valid cells; 11 of 36 cells dropped as no-data in at least one map. Means differ by design (A \u2248 0.10, B \u2248 0.68), but per the tool's warning those figures don't measure a gap between the maps.\n\n| Item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Cells compared / dropped | 25 / 11 (no-data) |\n| Correlation (A vs B) | -0.0172 (essentially none) |\n| RMSE / agreement fraction | 0.618 / 0.0 (not meaningful across properties) |\n\n**Which is right:** I can't say. This is model-vs-model agreement with no ground truth \u2014 neither output has labels in your Studio account, so accuracy/verified change isn't resolvable from these two maps alone. To settle it you'd need labeled karst samples for part of the AOI; I can then design a label-budget plan and compute real error rates per model. Want me to set that up?", "forced_by_turn_cap": false, "seq": 14, "t": 127.492, "seconds": 8.395}
